course: dictionary
lesson: 12809
title: Nature words: elm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An elm is a tall tree. It has rough, oval leaves with jagged edges, which means the edges are uneven, like tiny saw teeth. The word elm can also mean the hard wood that comes from this tree. «We sat in the shade of a big elm tree.» Here elm means the tree.
explain: «The table was made of elm, so it is hard and strong.» Here elm means the wood, not the tree. How do you know? The sentence tells you the table is made of it, and you cannot make a table out of a whole tree standing in a field. Always check the words around the word to see which meaning fits.
explain: Elms often grow in rows along old roads and village greens. «Old elms line the road to the village.» Line here means they stand in a row beside the road. Many elms in Europe and North America were lost to a disease spread by beetles, so old elms are now quite rare.
fact: An elm is a tall tree with rough, oval leaves.
fact: The leaves of an elm have jagged edges, like tiny saw teeth.
fact: Elm is also the name of the hard wood from this tree.
fact: «An avenue of elms» means a row of elm trees along a road.
fact: Many elms died from Dutch elm disease, a disease spread by beetles, so old elms are now rarer.
exercise: «We sat in the shade of a big elm tree.» What is an elm? | A road full of cars | A kind of bird that sings at night | A small flower that smells sweet | *A tall tree with rough, oval leaves
exercise: «The table was made of elm, so it is hard and strong.» What does elm mean in this sentence? | A tall tower | A sort of leaf | A village green | *The hard wood from the tree
exercise: «The leaves had jagged edges, like tiny saw teeth.» What does jagged mean? | Soft and round | Very long and thin | *Rough and uneven, with sharp points | Smooth and shiny
test: Many elms died from a disease spread by beetles. Why are old elms rarer now? | Too many people climbed them and broke them | *Many died from a disease spread by beetles | They grew too tall to see | They were cut down to make paper
test: What does «an avenue of elms» mean? | A big bowl of soup | A river under a bridge | *A row of elm trees along a road | A tall tower in a town
exam: Which sentence uses elm to mean the wood? | *The new shelf is made of elm, so it is strong. | We sat under an elm and ate our lunch. | Old elms line the road to the village. | The elms on the green were very tall.
